<title>SWEDEN: Trelleborg posts sharp fall 9 mo profit.</title>
<headline>Trelleborg posts sharp fall 9 mo profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish mining company Trelleborg reports for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		    837 vs  3,168</p>
<p> Sales					15,291 vs 15,820</p>
<p> Shr after tax (crowns)		   5.05 vs  22.10</p>
<p> Operating costs			  14,199 vs 15,737</p>
<p> Operating income			 15,399 vs 19,196</p>
<p> Depreciation				  572 vs    569</p>
<p> Net financial items		CREDIT 132 vs    311 CHARGE</p>
<p> Interest in other companies		77 vs    589</p>
<p> Minorities					0 vs     10 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     245 vs    566</p>
<p> Net profit				    592 vs  2,592</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll of analysts found an market consensus for a profit after financial items of 891 million crown for the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
